 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-1053) '| Internal   | `.usdc`, and `.usda` to read |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1053  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-1053) '| Avatar out | VRM, or KHR avatar           |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1053  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-1053) '| Asset out  | glTF binary                  |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1053  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-1053) '| Archive    | `.usdz`                      |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1053  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-1053) 'Convert at the boundary only. A stage that converts in the middle throws away the composition this RFD exists to keep.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1053  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-1053) 'Worlds
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1053  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-1053) 'A world is a USD stage as well. Its root layer names a spawn point and sublayers the environment and the props; each prop is a prim with its mesh, transform and interaction type. The avatar, the world and its props stay in separate layers, so loading one never replaces another.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1053  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-1053) 'The runtime
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1053  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-1053) '`fabric-stage-runtime` ships OpenUSD 26.5.0 as an Elixir Hex package. It exposes `include_dir/0`, `lib_dir/0`, and `target/0`, thus every consumer links the same USD build the model images write. (An earlier draft named "the Elixir core from RFD 1019" as the consumer; RFD66606-2169 abandoned that plan, and the Hex package survives without the studio-core wrapper.)
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1053  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-1053) 'One USD version across the pipeline matters. A layer written by a newer build may not open in an older one.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1053  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-1053) 'What each model image must do
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1053  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-1053) '`predict()` returns the USD layer, and it returns the transmission file as well. The caller keeps the layer, and it ships the other.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1053  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-1053) 'RFD66606-1036 records this in the model image convention.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1053  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-1053) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1053  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-1053) 'Every rewrite loses what came before. glTF holds one flat result, thus a stage cannot add an opinion without erasing the previous author.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1053  1 LINE
 Text:Written
